boldly:
Their warm, heart-melting motions to be wooed;
And passion boldly rising in my breast,
Like rivers of the Spring, lets loose its flood.

bolder:
And the same ardors in my soul should burn:
Then should my song in bolder notes arise,
And all my numbers pleasingly surprise;

And winter comes which is yet colder;
Each day the hoar-frost waxes bolder,
And the last buds cease blowing.

bolts:
They have fooled the man with lies;
The bolts unbar, the locks are drawn,
And the great door open flies.

bole:
Dance through the fairy neem;
From the poppy-bole
For you I stole
